WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.145
Heat the oven to 425°F. Halve the baby potatoes, wash the broccoli, and keep raw chicken on a separate tray.

00:00:10.145 --> 00:00:19.085
Season chicken and potatoes with paprika, salt and pepper. Melt the butter with garlic, then coat the chicken and potatoes.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:29.235
Place chicken and potatoes on a sheet pan. Roast at 425°F for 15 minutes before adding the broccoli.

00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:38.235
Add broccoli to the pan. Roast 10–15 minutes more. Cooking time varies with chicken thickness and potato size.

00:00:38.235 --> 00:00:49.702
Check the thickest part of the chicken with a food thermometer. It must reach 165°F. Continue cooking as needed until potatoes are tender.

00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:58.457
Rest the chicken for 5 minutes. Serve with roasted potatoes and broccoli, spooning the pan juices over each plate.

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:10.807
For four servings, mix 2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil, 1 tablespoon chopped parsley and 1 teaspoon lemon zest. Drizzle lightly over the plated dish.
